    {
      "id": "201d99ea-277c-53b8-ab20-df904af221ac",
      "document_id": "tech/tpp-standards/security/fapi",
      "type": "subsection",
      "text": "FAPI Security Profile > Key Security Mechanisms > The four pillars of FAPI 2.0 in UAE Open Finance > Signed Request Objects (JAR)\n\nThe body of the /par request must be a signed JWT — a JSON Web Signature (JWS). This is a cryptographically signed package of claims that proves:\n\n- Authenticity — the request genuinely came from your registered application\n- Integrity — no parameter was modified in transit\n\nSee Preparing the Request JWT for the full structure.",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "FAPI Security Profile",
        "section": "The four pillars of FAPI 2.0 in UAE Open Finance",
        "category": "Key Security Mechanisms",
        "subsection": "Signed Request Objects (JAR)",
        "anchor": "mechanisms",
        "source_repo": "Nebras-Open-Finance/community-standards",
        "source_file": "src/pages/tech/tpp-standards/security/fapi/index.vue",
        "parser": "vue-sfc",
        "source_commit": "67e5ca444c9ee40e4624fe6ea88d382e62c0d50f",
        "source_hash": "94ea96d633375e41183133f6da7536bc803d9be92d10d14204aa82324e1c6077",
        "url": "https://nebras-open-finance.com/tech/tpp-standards/security/fapi",
