    {
      "id": "1c364ba0-4c3b-5d5a-b393-7ade31ff2de9",
      "document_id": "tech/tpp-standards/security/fapi",
      "type": "subsection",
      "text": "FAPI Security Profile > Key Security Mechanisms > The four pillars of FAPI 2.0 in UAE Open Finance > PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange)\n\nEvery authorization request includes a code_challenge derived from a secret code_verifier. When the authorization code is later exchanged for tokens, the code_verifier must be provided. This prevents authorization code interception attacks.\n\nThe only supported method is S256 (SHA-256 hash of the verifier).",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "FAPI Security Profile",
        "section": "The four pillars of FAPI 2.0 in UAE Open Finance",
        "category": "Key Security Mechanisms",
        "subsection": "PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange)",
        "anchor": "mechanisms",
        "source_repo": "Nebras-Open-Finance/community-standards",
        "source_file": "src/pages/tech/tpp-standards/security/fapi/index.vue",
        "parser": "vue-sfc",
        "source_commit": "67e5ca444c9ee40e4624fe6ea88d382e62c0d50f",
