    {
      "id": "59b4c911-0c4f-5052-8fb7-0a76bb63aeb1",
      "document_id": "tech/tpp-standards/security/fapi",
      "type": "subsection",
      "text": "FAPI Security Profile > Key Security Mechanisms > The four pillars of FAPI 2.0 in UAE Open Finance > mTLS (Mutual TLS)\n\nAll API requests use mutual TLS — both client and server present certificates during the TLS handshake. Your application must present its transport certificate (issued by the Trust Framework) to authenticate at the network level.\n\nThis ensures that even a stolen access token cannot be used without the corresponding private key.",
      "metadata": {
        "title": "FAPI Security Profile",
        "section": "The four pillars of FAPI 2.0 in UAE Open Finance",
        "category": "Key Security Mechanisms",
        "subsection": "mTLS (Mutual TLS)",
        "anchor": "mechanisms",
        "source_repo": "Nebras-Open-Finance/community-standards",
